# Database operations

- Run from repository root with one root .env. APP_ENV local|dev|uat|prod selects the Compose environment. Use Bash for .sh scripts and Git Bash on Windows.
- Use scripts/database/initialize.mjs with DB_SCHEMA_SYNC_APPROVED=true for an empty database. It reads only database/schema.sql; never resets or upgrades an existing mismatched database.
- SEED_PATH must be database/seeds/sql-master. All contents are private and gitignored; never force-add them. Do not create another seed source or edit private datasets for testing.
- scripts/database/seed.mjs executes numbered SQL INSERT files atomically on an empty initialized database. Keep source UUIDs/timestamps and align identity sequences. RUN_SEED defaults false; disable it after first seed.
- db-manage.sh/.ps1 supports status, connect, logs, seed, backup, restore, health and prune-backups. reset and force-seed are refused.
- Backup uses scripts/database/backup.mjs: custom pg_dump + checksum/inventory + disposable restore verification. restore is an isolated rehearsal, never a live overwrite. Preserve pinned archives and the newest verified backup.
- Before live schema changes, obtain a fresh verified baseline and explicit cutover approval. Never reset, migrate, seed or deploy a used database just to satisfy a test.
- Run pnpm test:database-docker against disposable containers only. No production mounts, real tokens, or implicit live DB connections.
